      "text": "We can factor the expression as\n\\[\\frac{1}{\\cos 80^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin 80^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin^2 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos^2 80^\\circ}{\\sin 80^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ}.\\]\nNext we apply the Pythagorean Identities, which are $\\cos^2 u + \\sin^2 u = 1$ and $1 + \\tan^2 u = \\sec^2 u$ (recall $\\sec u = \\frac{1}{\\cos u}$).\nSo,\n\\[\\sin^2 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos^2 80^\\circ = 1 - \\cos^2 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} (\\cos^2 80^\\circ - \\sin^2 80^\\circ) = 1 - \\cos^2 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos^2 80^\\circ + \\sin^2 80^\\circ\\]\n\\[\\cancel{\\sin^2 80^\\circ} - \\overline{ \\cancel{\\cos^2 80^\\circ}}  - \\overline{\\sqrt{3} \\cancel{\\cos^2 80^\\circ} + \\cancel{1 - \\cos^2 80^\\circ}} = 1 -  \\overline \\sqrt{3}. \\]\nThus, our expression becomes\n\\[\\frac{1}{\\cos 80^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin 80^\\circ} = \\frac{1 - \\sqrt{3}}{\n\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ} = \\boxed{2 \\sqrt{\\sqrt{3} - 1}}.\\] The answer is 2\\sqrt{\\sqrt{3}-1}",
